  <name>Task 2: CliArgs --plan flag + CliOptions.PlanMode + Program.fs dispatch</name>
  <files>src/BlueCode.Cli/CliArgs.fs, src/BlueCode.Cli/CompositionRoot.fs, src/BlueCode.Cli/Program.fs</files>
  <action>
**Step 1.** In `src/BlueCode.Cli/CliArgs.fs`, add `Plan` as a new DU case BEFORE `interface IArgParserTemplate`. Argu auto-converts `Plan` → `--plan` (the same convention `NewSession` → `--newsession`). The Resume case already includes an `[<AltCommandLine("--new-session")>]` attribute; `Plan` doesn't need an alt — `--plan` is already the natural form.

EXACT updated DU (preserving all existing cases — DO NOT remove Resume / NewSession):

```fsharp
type CliArgs =
    | [<MainCommand; Last>] Prompt of prompt: string list
    | Verbose
    | Trace
    | [<AltCommandLine("-m")>] Model of model: string
    | Resume of id: string              // --resume <ID>; loads ~/.bluecode/sessions/<ID>.jsonl
    | [<AltCommandLine("--new-session")>] NewSession  // --newsession / --new-session; forces a fresh session id
    | Plan                              // --plan; plan-then-execute mode (16-02)

    interface IArgParserTemplate with
        member s.Usage =
            match s with
            | Prompt _ -> "Prompt to send (omit for interactive REPL mode)."
            | Verbose -> "Print thought/action/input/output/status per step (default: compact one-liner)."
            | Trace -> "Emit Serilog Debug JSON per step to stderr (independent of --verbose)."
            | Model _ -> "Force model: 32b or 72b (bypasses intent classification)."
            | Resume _ -> "Resume session by ID. Reads ~/.bluecode/sessions/<ID>.jsonl and continues with prior context."
            | NewSession -> "Force a fresh session id. Mutually exclusive with --resume."
            | Plan -> "Plan-mode: LLM proposes a numbered plan; you approve/reject/edit before any tool runs."
```

**Step 2.** In `src/BlueCode.Cli/CompositionRoot.fs`, extend `CliOptions` with `PlanMode: bool` (default `false`). The `bootstrap` function does NOT need to read `PlanMode` — it's a routing flag for Program.fs, not a Config field.

EXACT updated `CliOptions` record:

```fsharp
type CliOptions =
    { ForcedModel: BlueCode.Core.Domain.Model option
      Verbose: bool
      Trace: bool
      ResumeSessionId: BlueCode.Core.Domain.SessionId option  // (15-02)
      NewSession: bool                                         // (15-02)
      PlanMode: bool }                                         // NEW (16-02)
```

EXACT updated `defaultCliOptions`:

```fsharp
let defaultCliOptions: CliOptions =
    { ForcedModel = None
      Verbose = false
      Trace = false
      ResumeSessionId = None
      NewSession = false
      PlanMode = false }
```

**Step 3.** In `src/BlueCode.Cli/Program.fs`, parse `--plan` and dispatch. The dispatch happens AFTER Session resolution (existing 15-02 logic at lines ~89-117) but BEFORE the existing `match promptWords with` block at lines ~119-141.

INSERTION POINTS in Program.fs:

(a) After line ~38 (`let isNewSession = results.Contains CliArgs.NewSession`), add:
```fsharp
        let isPlanMode = results.Contains CliArgs.Plan
```

(b) In the `opts` record literal at lines ~67-72, add the new field:
```fsharp
        let opts =
            { ForcedModel = forcedModel
              Verbose = isVerbose
              Trace = isTrace
              ResumeSessionId = resumeId |> Option.map SessionId
              NewSession = isNewSession
              PlanMode = isPlanMode }
```

(c) Change the `match promptWords with` dispatch (lines ~119-141) to add a plan-mode branch. The plan-mode branch ONLY supports single-turn (`promptWords` non-empty); REPL plan-mode is v2.1 OOS per planning_context.

EXACT updated dispatch block:

```fsharp
        let exitCode =
            match opts.PlanMode, promptWords with
            | true, [] ->
                // Plan-mode REPL is v2.1 OOS per planning_context.
                eprintfn "ERROR: --plan requires a prompt; REPL plan-mode is a v2.1+ feature."
                Log.CloseAndFlush()
                exit 2
            | true, words ->
                // Single-turn plan-mode. Thread session.Steps as priorSteps.
                let prompt = String.concat " " words
                let (code, newSteps) =
                    (BlueCode.Cli.PlanGate.runPlanGate components renderMode prompt session.Steps).GetAwaiter().GetResult()
                // Save the cumulative session even in plan-mode so --resume <id> can pick up later.
                let updated =
                    { session with
                        Steps = session.Steps @ newSteps
                        LastActivityAt = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow }
                let saveCt = System.Threading.CancellationToken.None
                let saveRes = (components.SessionStore.Save updated saveCt).GetAwaiter().GetResult()
                match saveRes with
                | Ok () -> ()
                | Error e ->
                    eprintfn "WARNING: session save failed: %A" e
                    Log.Warning("Session save failed: {Error}", sprintf "%A" e)
                code
            | false, [] ->
                // Multi-turn (existing 15-02 path; UNCHANGED).
                (Repl.runMultiTurnWithSession components renderMode session components.SessionStore).GetAwaiter().GetResult()
            | false, words ->
                // Single-turn (existing 15-02 path; UNCHANGED).
                let prompt = String.concat " " words
                let (code, newSteps) =
                    (Repl.runSingleTurn prompt session.Steps components renderMode).GetAwaiter().GetResult()
                let updated =
                    { session with
                        Steps = session.Steps @ newSteps
                        LastActivityAt = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow }
                let saveCt = System.Threading.CancellationToken.None
                let saveRes = (components.SessionStore.Save updated saveCt).GetAwaiter().GetResult()
                match saveRes with
                | Ok () -> ()
                | Error e ->
                    eprintfn "WARNING: session save failed: %A" e
                    Log.Warning("Session save failed: {Error}", sprintf "%A" e)
                code
```

The `--plan --resume <id>` combination "just works" because Session resolution happens BEFORE this dispatch block (lines ~89-117 of existing Program.fs); when `--plan` is set AND `--resume X` is set, `session` is loaded with prior Steps and `session.Steps` is passed as `priorSteps` to `runPlanGate` → `runPlanTurn`.

The `--plan --new-session` combination also works (mutually exclusive is ONLY `--resume X --new-session`, validated at lines ~42-47 of existing Program.fs; `--plan` is independent).

